          }
        },
        "care_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Care & Maintenance",
            "size": "large",
            "append_product_title": false
          }
        },
        "care_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Keep your Yosukata carbon steel wok in excellent condition with proper cleaning, seasoning, and storage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "care_first_use_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Before First Use",
            "size": "small",
            "append_product_title": false
          }
        },
        "care_first_use": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Although your Yosukata wok is pre-seasoned, it requires additional seasoning with oil before cooking. Wash it thoroughly with warm, soapy water to remove any protective oil or residue from manufacturing and shipping. Dry completely, then apply a thin, even layer of cooking oil and season according to the manufacturer's instructions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "care_cleaning_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Cleaning & Maintenance",
            "size": "small",
            "append_product_title": false
          }
        },
        "care_cleaning": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Allow the wok to cool before cleaning. Hand-wash with warm water and a soft sponge to remove food residue. A small amount of mild dish soap can be used when necessary, but avoid harsh detergents and abrasive scrubbing that may damage the seasoning.</p><p>Never place the wok in a dishwasher or leave it soaking in water, as prolonged moisture exposure can cause rust.</p>"
          }
        },
        "care_drying_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Drying & Storage",
            "size": "small",
            "append_product_title": false
          }
        },
        "care_drying": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Immediately after washing, dry the wok thoroughly with a clean towel or over low heat to remove any remaining moisture.</p><p>Before storing, apply a very thin layer of cooking oil to protect the carbon steel surface from oxidation. Store in a clean, dry, well-ventilated place, away from excessive humidity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "care_seasoning_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Seasoning & Long-Term Care",
            "size": "small",
            "append_product_title": false
          }
        },
        "care_seasoning": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>With regular use, your wok will gradually develop a darker, more effective natural non-stick patina. Changes in surface color and uneven darkening are normal characteristics of carbon steel.</p><p>If food begins to stick or rust appears, gently remove the affected residue or rust and re-season the surface with cooking oil.</p><p>Avoid leaving acidic foods or sauces in the wok for extended periods, as they can weaken the protective seasoning layer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "care_video_heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to Season",
            "size": "large",
            "append_product_title": true
          }
        },
        "care_video": {
          "type": "media",
          "settings": {
            "video_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JzKLXxAxrzw",
            "video_title": "How to season a wok (basic oil method)",
            "width": "full",
            "default_asset": "yk-product-care.jpg"
          }
        },
        "tab_shipping": {
